 The Large Load meets all frequency ride-through requirements, voltage ride 
through requirements, post-fault active power recovery requirements, and ramp 
rate limitations in accordance with CAISO Tariff Sections 25.7.1.1, 25.7.1.2, 
25.7.1.3, and 25.7.1.4.  This ensures no Large Load is energized until the 
information and equipment necessary to preserve reliability and to operate 
consistent with CAISO requirements is in place. 
H. 
Ministerial and Conforming Revisions 
GridLiance West has also made several ministerial or conforming revisions to either 
clarify or correct its tariff language or to better clarify the GridLiance West Tariff’s relation to the 
CAISO Tariff.  These include: 
 Updating the Cover Sheet, including the Table of Contents; 
 Clarifying in Section 1 that GridLiance West does not provide retail electric 
service; 
 Clarifying in Section 1.3 how End-Users access the CAISO Controlled Grid; 
 Updating the definition of Ancillary Services in Section 3.3; 
 Updating the definition of Available Transfer Capacity in Section 3.5; 
 Updating the definition of Congestion Management in Section 3.13;  
 Updating the definition of Dispatch in Section 3.18; 
 Updating the definition of End-Use Customer or End-User in Section 3.22; 
 Updating the definition of Generating Unit in Section 3.33; 
 Updating the definition of Good Utility Practice in Section 3.35; 
 Updating the definition of Interest in Section 3.51 to align with CAISO Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Local Publicly Owned Electric Utility in Section 3.54; 
 Updating the definition of Metered Subsystem in Section 3.61; 
 Updating the definition of Non-Load-Serving Participating TO in Section 3.66 to 
align with CAISO Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Non-Spinning Reserve in Section 3.68 to align with 
CAISO Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Spinning Reserve in Section 3.87 to align with CAISO 
Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Utility Distribution Company in Section 3.99; 
 Defining FILI Service in Section 3.31 consistent with the CAISO Tariff; 
 Clarifying Gross Load’s definition in Section 3.36 to better match CAISO; 
 Revising the definition of “Interconnection” in Section 3.47 to address a 
typographical error; 
 Defining Interconnection Facilities in Section 3.50 to provide clarity; 
 Defining Point of Interconnection in Section 3.74 to align with CAISO; 
 Revising the definition of Reliability Upgrade in Section 3.82 to refer to a 
“facility” rather than an undefined term; 
 Ministerial additions of subsections and headers throughout Sections 8, 9, and 10 
to enhance readability of the tariff for customers and stakeholders; 
 Retitling Section 13 “Creditworthiness and Financial Security”;
